                <pb facs="0790" n="710" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg710"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hill to Lord Pauncefote.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-04-12"><hi rendition="#italic">April 12,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">Personal.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Ambassador</hi>: I inclose a memorandum
                    in reply to the one inclosed with your personal note of the 8th instant in
                    regard to the proposed arbitration of the question of the Japanese Government’s
                    right to the imposition of the house tax in respect of buildings which are held
                    under perpetual leases.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">David J. Hill.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
